                                        <div class="tab-pane fade" id="pills-4" role="tabpanel" aria-labelledby="Director&#39;sMessage"  ><p>Since its inception in 1986, School of Sciences has continuously evolved with respect to the number of programmes offered and increasing enrolment. The school offers various programmes at Bachelor's, Master’s and Doctoral levels through its 8 Disciplines. The learners enrolled in various programmes, drawn from all over the country have been continuously increasing, attesting to the acceptability of the programmes designed and developed by the dynamic Faculty of the School. Our UG and PG programmes have been designed to cater the diverse requirements and aspirations of our learner spread across the country. The school has persistently pursued its objectives with changing times with updating academic programmes and curriculum. Our curriculum is updated to equip our learners with the domain knowledge, foundation and skills enhancement courses. Faculty has relentlessly striven to design and develop Masters’ programmes in Biochemistry, Chemistry, Analytical Chemistry, Geography, Geoinformatics, Applied Statistics, Physics and Zoology in conformity with NEP 2020. The School was awarded ‘Best School Award’ on the 38th Foundation Day of the University for launching eight PG programmes and one PG Diploma programme during the year 2023. School has launched PG and UG programmes in 2024 under FYUP-UGC scheme in accordance with NEP 2020. </p>

<p>Automatic Weather Station (AWS) has been installed in IGNOU campus at Maidan Garhi as the consequence of MOU signed between IGNOU and Meteorological Department (IMD) in 2023. Research undertaken at School of Sciences has gained momentum with faculty and students publishing widely in peer-reviewed journals and making their presence felt at conferences and workshops, within the country and abroad. It is needless to mention that with the vast experience of more than three decades, and available expertise, the school will successfully fulfill its stated objectives in the times to come</p></div>
